insert_before("loader", dict(
    slug="rendering-engine", title="3D engine & particles", category="Media",
    image="home-operator-verified.png", table="rendering",
    summary="The model chapter uses Three.js point clouds; operator characters use pre-rendered alpha video.",
    facts=[("Renderer", "Three.js / WebGL"), ("Models", "Six Float32Array .bin clouds"),
           ("Scan width", "20 scene units"), ("Quality", "10k-point benchmark")],
    paragraphs=[
      "There are two different rendering systems. Operator character movement is delivered as 33 pairs of pre-rendered enter and idle MP4 clips, composited with alpha data; those are not browser-rendered 3D character meshes. A separate model/environment chapter creates a Three.js scene. It fetches six binary point clouds, reads them as Float32Array positions, normalizes their height to about 1900 scene units, and attaches per-point random size, layer and timing data.",
      "The live scene uses WebGLRenderer with antialias and alpha, a PerspectiveCamera with FOV 75, near .1, far 10000 and z=2000, and transparent shader-driven Points geometry. Three scan lines pass through the cloud; points near a line turn yellowish while distant points remain grey and fade. The fragment shader discards pixels beyond a radial threshold, softens edges and adds an inner glow. Instanced laser rays and periodic glitch offsets give the engineered scan look. The shipped binary path reads raw floats; no client-side decryption step was observed.",
      "Performance is part of the visual rule. The code times an offscreen 10,000-point render: over 30ms downgrades one tier, over 60ms a second tier. Tiers change ray batches (20, 14 or 8), maximum rays (2000, 1000 or 500) and at the lowest quality set pixel ratio to .75. The scene rotates about .005 rad per frame and drag adds about .01 rad per pixel with eased interpolation. A child site can retain the scan-line particle grammar with its own model data, but should isolate WebGL so the archive and basic navigation never depend on it."],
    rules=["Keep character footage and real-time WebGL as two explicit media services.",
           "Budget particles and ray instances from an actual device benchmark.",
           "Pause rendering when the scene is hidden and offer a static fallback."],
    code="fetch(modelBin).then(r=>r.arrayBuffer()).then(b=>new Float32Array(b));\ngeometry.setAttribute('position', positions);\ngeometry.setAttribute('pointMoreData', extras);\nrenderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({antialias:true,alpha:true});"
))

